<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27388" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lyncus</span></b> , i, = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λύγκος</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Masc., a Scythian king, who attempted the life of
				his guest, Triptolemus, and was changed by Ceres into a
			lynx</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 5, 650</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab.
				259</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Fem., a city of Macedonia, the capital of the</i>
			Lyncestae (q. v.), <i><span class="en">Liv. 26, 25, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">31, 33</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
